+## What this records
+
+**ADR 067: when no plan file marks a feature's story, a play finds it by the issue the product model names, and never by title.** All plan files were deleted on 2026-11-02 (#1021), so a plan file's mark finds nothing. The decision gives the model's link a defined meaning. An open story is used, and moved under the slice's epic with the move shown before the yes. A closed story means the feature is already built: no new story is made. The review of PR #1047 (#1025) found the code conflicted with ADR 056 §2, and this decision resolves that. Accepted by the product owner on 2026-11-12 through /design-adr.
+
+Closes #1048
+
+## How to review it
+
+- `docs/adr/067-...md`: the record.
+- ADRs 056, 048 and 049: each gets one forward pointer on its Status line and nothing else.
+- `docs/adr/_index.md`: rebuilt.
+- Everything else is run records under the issue folders. Two of them are copies of the ontology and the ADR template, kept as evidence.
+- Follow-up: the ontology change (a Feature gets an `issue`) goes through /specify-ontology. PR #1047 lands after this one.
+
+## Self-review
+
